          "id": "2122500307557265651",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "@simonw The credential-replacement proxy is the underrated part. A sandbox stops rm -rf; it doesn't stop an agent holding a real API key from leaking it to an allowed host. Keys outside + egress allow-list + sandboxed exec = actual defense in depth.",
      "url": "https://x.com/AIAgentsIn5/status/2122837670443291006"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1858474496203911168",
